\subsection{Tie Rate as Structural Property}
\label{sec:tie_rate}

Across all four judge--axis configurations, Likert tie rates cluster in the 58--73\% range: GPT-4o formality 62.5\%, Qwen3-32B formality 72.7\%, Qwen3-32B verbosity 58.1\%, Qwen3-32B register 63.8\%.
This consistency across architecturally distinct judges and different style axes supports the interpretation that high tie rates are a structural property of integer Likert scales, not a judge-specific artifact.
The tie rate acts as the first layer of the Blindspot mechanism: before any statistical test is applied, the majority of the evaluation budget is lost to uninformative ties.

